<GuideContainer>
    <Section Title="Overview">
        <Explanation>
            <p>
                <strong>Ardeos</strong> is a ranged spellcaster who specialises in
                damage-over-time. The core of the kit is layering as many burning
                effects on your targets as possible, then converting that pressure
                into burst by managing <strong>Cinders</strong> and
                <strong>Embers</strong> to fuel <strong>Detonate</strong>.
            </p>
        </Explanation>
        <TipBox Variant="TipBoxVariant.Note" Title="ABC — Always Be Casting">
            The fundamental skill gap on Ardeos is dead time between casts. Mark your
            targets with keybinds and use the HUD editor to move buff/debuff displays
            toward the centre of the screen so you can always see what needs refreshing.
        </TipBox>
    </Section>

    <Section Title="Core Mechanic — Cinders &amp; Embers">
        <Explanation>
            <p>
                Your damage-over-time effects generate <strong>Cinders</strong>. At
                100 Cinders you gain an <strong>Ember</strong>, which is spent on
                <strong>Detonate</strong>. Detonate's damage scales with the
                <em>number</em> of active DoTs on the target (not their remaining
                duration), and it does <em>not</em> consume those DoTs — so the more
                burns you have running when you Detonate, the harder it hits.
            </p>
            <p>
                Cinders come from <strong>Searing Blaze</strong>,
                <strong>Engulfing Flames</strong>, and <strong>Fire Ball</strong>
                DoTs, as well as <strong>Infernal Wave</strong> casts.
                <strong>Fire Ball</strong> generates Cinders per tick, which makes it
                a key AoE generator, while <strong>Infernal Wave</strong> is your
                primary spammable Cinder generator between burn windows.
            </p>
        </Explanation>
        <TipBox Variant="TipBoxVariant.Note" Title="Don't overcap">
            Cast <strong>Detonate</strong> as you approach the Ember cap. Sitting at
            cap wastes the Cinders you keep generating, so spend before you overflow.
        </TipBox>
    </Section>

    <Section Title="Rotation">
        <SubSection Title="Single-Target Burn Window">
            <Explanation>
                <p>Build the burn window before you spam <strong>Detonate</strong>:</p>
                <ol>
                    <li><strong>Fire Frogs</strong></li>
                    <li><strong>Apocalypse</strong></li>
                    <li><strong>Fire Ball</strong></li>
                    <li><strong>Engulfing Flames</strong> x2</li>
                    <li><strong>Pyromania</strong></li>
                    <li><strong>Wildfire</strong></li>
                    <li><strong>Detonate</strong> spam</li>
                </ol>
            </Explanation>
        </SubSection>

        <SubSection Title="AoE Burn Window (multiple targets)">
            <Explanation>
                <p>
                    Run the same burn-window spine, swapping the opener for a
                    wide <strong>Searing Blaze</strong> application when
                    <strong>Apocalypse</strong> is unavailable:
                </p>
                <ol>
                    <li><strong>Fire Frogs</strong></li>
                    <li><strong>Searing Blaze</strong> — spread to as many targets as possible in place of <strong>Apocalypse</strong></li>
                    <li><strong>Fire Ball</strong> — per-tick Cinders make this your key AoE generator</li>
                    <li><strong>Engulfing Flames</strong> x2 — cast frequently with <strong>Rolling Flames</strong></li>
                    <li><strong>Pyromania</strong></li>
                    <li><strong>Wildfire</strong></li>
                    <li><strong>Detonate</strong> spam</li>
                </ol>
            </Explanation>
        </SubSection>

        <SubSection Title="Maintenance (Between Burns)">
            <Explanation>
                <ul>
                    <li>Refresh <strong>Searing Blaze</strong> as it expires.</li>
                    <li>Spam <strong>Infernal Wave</strong> to build Cinders.</li>
                    <li>Cast <strong>Detonate</strong> when approaching the Ember cap to avoid waste.</li>
                </ul>
            </Explanation>
        </SubSection>

        <SubSection Title="Ultimate Combo — Incinerate Burst">
            <Explanation>
                <p>
                    Deploy <strong>Incinerate</strong> just before
                    <strong>Wildfire</strong>, after your DoTs are applied. It extends
                    all current DoTs ahead of <strong>Wildfire</strong> and
                    <strong>Detonate</strong> for maximum burst.
                </p>
            </Explanation>
        </SubSection>

        <SubSection Title="Advanced Chronoshift Combo (Single-Target)">
            <Explanation>
                <p>
                    With <strong>Asha's Chronoshift Spire</strong> and 4/4
                    <strong>Visions Of Grandeur</strong>, extend two full burn windows
                    back-to-back:
                </p>
                <ol>
                    <li><strong>Fire Frogs</strong></li>
                    <li><strong>Apocalypse</strong></li>
                    <li><strong>Fire Ball</strong></li>
                    <li><strong>Engulfing Flames</strong> x2</li>
                    <li><strong>Pyromania</strong></li>
                    <li><strong>Wildfire</strong></li>
                    <li><strong>Chronoshift</strong></li>
                    <li><strong>Engulfing Flames</strong> (x2 if possible)</li>
                    <li><strong>Fire Ball</strong></li>
                    <li><strong>Incinerate</strong></li>
                    <li><strong>Chronoshift</strong></li>
                    <li><strong>Apocalypse</strong></li>
                    <li><strong>Engulfing Flames</strong> (x2 if possible)</li>
                    <li><strong>Wildfire</strong></li>
                    <li><strong>Detonate</strong> spam</li>
                </ol>
            </Explanation>
        </SubSection>
    </Section>

    <Section Title="Cooldowns &amp; Utility">
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Flame Ward</strong> — 40% damage reduction on a 30s cooldown.</li>
            <li><strong>Fireflash</strong> — single-target disorient to stop dangerous mob casts.</li>
        </ul>
    </Section>

    <Section Title="Talents &amp; Builds">
        <Explanation>
            <p>
                <strong>Reign Of Fire</strong> grants <strong>Fire Ball</strong>
                charges with enhanced casts — use the effect as soon as it triggers to
                avoid overcapping charges.
            </p>
            <p>
                <strong>Rolling Flames</strong> reduces the cooldown of
                <strong>Engulfing Flames</strong>. In AoE, cast it frequently without
                waiting to reach 2 charges; in single-target it enables smaller burn
                windows between <strong>Wildfire</strong> phases.
            </p>
        </Explanation>
    </Section>

